From 12f24c09a1a6db7a2a47a8aa403ec551c6a53938 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ksg <sisungaa851@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:21:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bent and twisted joints across exercise demonstrations

- Point solved elbows backwards so walking and hanging arms no longer
  hyperextend; blend stretch forearms in the upper-arm frame.
- Rest prone, kneeling and child-pose feet on the instep instead of a
  180-degree yaw that twisted the ankle.
- Use overhand grips for barbell lifts, presses and RDLs, and rotate the
  pressing humerus into the elbow's flexion plane so the skin no longer
  crumples at the elbow.
- Square the raised single-bridge foot, flex side-plank knees backwards,
  rest seated palms on the thighs and lay the clamshell forearm on the mat.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
